{
  "message": "The good news is that the emulation found no failures. The design is wired end to end and keeps the read-only, no-apply boundary, so the blockers are unfinished work rather than broken logic. The first actionable finding is that the inventory bucket has no explicit access contract, meaning nobody is recorded as allowed to put synthetic snapshots into it. The other seven blockers are missing native implementations for Step Functions, the Lambdas, DynamoDB, CloudTrail and the existing-system references, so those are product engineering work, not diagram fixes.\n\nWho should load the synthetic snapshots and baselines into that bucket: should the platform operator have read and write access to it, or should someone else upload them?",
